{"version":"6.9","hitCount":91,"nextCursorMark":"AoIIQKiwcSg1NTU3OTY0Ng==","nextPageUrl":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=TITLE_ABS%3A%28tensor+decomposition+EEG%29&cursorMark=AoIIQKiwcSg1NTU3OTY0Ng%3D%3D&resultType=core&pageSize=3&format=json","request":{"queryString":"TITLE_ABS:(tensor decomposition EEG)","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":3,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"42082088","source":"MED","pmid":"42082088","doi":"10.1016/j.neuroimage.2026.121962","title":"Equivalence of modified k-means and tensor decomposition in EEG microstates: Implications for analysis and interpretation.","authorString":"Ro\u0161\u0165\u00e1kov\u00e1 Z, Rosipal R.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Ro\u0161\u0165\u00e1kov\u00e1 Z","lastName":"Ro\u0161\u0165\u00e1kov\u00e1","firstName":"Zuzana","initials":"Z","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0192-9626"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Institute of Measurement Science, Slovak Academy of Sciences, D\u00fabravsk\u00e1 cesta 9, Bratislava, 841 04, Slovakia. Electronic address: zuzana.rostakova@savba.sk."}]}},{"fullName":"Rosipal R","lastName":"Rosipal","firstName":"Roman","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Institute of Measurement Science, Slovak Academy of Sciences, D\u00fabravsk\u00e1 cesta 9, Bratislava, 841 04, Slovakia."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0192-9626"}]},"journalInfo":{"volume":"334","journalIssueId":4194344,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Jul","monthOfPublication":7,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Neuroimage","title":"NeuroImage","essn":"1095-9572","issn":"1053-8119","nlmid":"9215515","isoabbreviation":"Neuroimage"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-07-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"121962","abstractText":"In the resting state, the human brain quickly transitions among a limited set of quasi-stable states known as EEG microstates, which characterize brain spatio-temporal activity with high temporal resolution. EEG microstates are typically identified using a clustering algorithm that analyzes peaks in the EEG global field power. In this study, we focus on the modified k-means algorithm (modKM), one of the most commonly employed methods for detecting EEG microstates. We demonstrate, both theoretically and through simulation and real EEG data, its equivalence with a different method known as the Implicit Slice Canonical Decomposition (IMSCAND), which is a special kind of tensor decomposition for symmetric higher order arrays. This relationship opens new avenues for EEG microstate detection, interpretation, and analysis by utilizing tensor decomposition methods and related techniques.","affiliation":"Institute of Measurement Science, Slovak Academy of Sciences, D\u00fabravsk\u00e1 cesta 9, Bratislava, 841 04, Slovakia. Electronic address: zuzana.rostakova@savba.sk.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Brain","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Electroencephalography","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Algorithms"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Computer Simulation"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Signal Processing, Computer-Assisted"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Clustering Algorithms"}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Electroencephalogram Eeg","Eeg Microstates","Parallel Factor Analysis","Tensor Decomposition","Implicit Slice Canonical Decomposition","Modified K-means"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuroimage.2026.121962"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"N","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2026-07-16","dateOfCreation":"2026-05-04","dateOfRevision":"2026-07-16","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-05-02","firstPublicationDate":"2026-05-02","firstIndexDate":"2026-05-13","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"42638687","source":"MED","pmid":"42638687","doi":"10.1007/s11571-026-10531-2","title":"High-accuracy EEG-based driver fatigue detection using feature-coupled tensor decomposition for multimodal brain connectivity analysis.","authorString":"Yan T, Su H, Yang Z, Zhang A, Ma Y, Wang X, Wu Y, Yan L, Wang Y, Cao J.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Yan T","lastName":"Yan","firstName":"Tian","initials":"T","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Automation, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, 710049 China."}]}},{"fullName":"Su H","lastName":"Su","firstName":"Hechong","initials":"H","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"XJTU-POLIMI Joint School, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, 710049 China."}]}},{"fullName":"Yang Z","lastName":"Yang","firstName":"Zengyao","initials":"Z","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Mechanical Engineering, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, 710049 China."}]}},{"fullName":"Zhang A","lastName":"Zhang","firstName":"Aimin","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Automation, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, 710049 China."}]}},{"fullName":"Ma Y","lastName":"Ma","firstName":"Yidan","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Automation, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, 710049 China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang X","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"Xiaolong","initials":"X","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Automation, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, 710049 China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wu Y","lastName":"Wu","firstName":"Yue","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Automation, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, 710049 China."}]}},{"fullName":"Yan L","lastName":"Yan","firstName":"Li","initials":"L","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Shanghai 9Th People's Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine, Shanghai, 200011 China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang Y","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"Yichen","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Ruijin Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine, Shanghai, 200011 China."}]}},{"fullName":"Cao J","lastName":"Cao","firstName":"Jianfu","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Automation, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, 710049 China."}]}}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"20","journalIssueId":4047609,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Dec","monthOfPublication":12,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Cogn Neurodyn","title":"Cognitive neurodynamics","essn":"1871-4099","issn":"1871-4080","nlmid":"101306907","isoabbreviation":"Cogn Neurodyn"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-12-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"163","abstractText":"Driver fatigue is a major threat to road safety, and electroencephalography (EEG)-based monitoring offers an effective approach for assessing a driver's cognitive state. However, existing brain network feature-extraction methods often rely on single-modality connectivity metrics, which may not fully capture the complex multidimensional reorganization of neural dynamics during the transition to fatigue. To address this methodological gap, this study proposes a Feature-Coupled Tensor Decomposition (FCTD) framework for multimodal brain network analysis. The framework constructs independent high-order tensors for three complementary connectivity metrics: signal covariance (representing amplitude coupling), phase-locking value (representing phase synchronization), and Liang-Kleeman information flow (representing directed information transfer). Using Tucker decomposition, FCTD learns spatial bases at the scalp-electrode level and employs a cross-mapping strategy to integrate latent inter-modality dependencies. The proposed framework was evaluated on two publicly available driver fatigue EEG datasets. Under a chronological block-wise 10-fold cross-validation protocol designed to reduce the risk of temporal leakage, the method achieved average accuracies of 99.42% and 93.62% on Dataset 1 and Dataset 2, respectively. Leave-one-subject-out (LOSO) cross-validation on Dataset 2 yielded an accuracy of 75.18%, indicating that cross-subject generalization remains challenging under substantial inter-subject variability. By integrating complementary connectivity views, this study provides a computationally efficient framework with feature projections for multimodal EEG feature extraction in fatigue monitoring systems.","affiliation":"School of Automation, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, 710049 China.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Electroencephalography (EEG)","Driver Fatigue Detection","Multimodal Brain Network","Feature-coupled Tensor Decomposition"]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11571-026-10531-2"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"N","hasTextMinedTerms":"N","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2026-08-25","dateOfCreation":"2026-08-25","dateOfRevision":"2026-08-26","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-08-24","firstPublicationDate":"2026-08-24","firstIndexDate":"2026-08-26","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"PPR1230389","source":"PPR","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PPR1230389"]},"doi":"10.64898/2025.12.21.695795","title":"Low-Rank Tensor Decomposition for Cross-Bispectral Analysis of EEG Data","authorString":"Kaziki D, Engel AK, Nolte G.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Kaziki D","lastName":"Kaziki","firstName":"Dionysia","initials":"D","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurophysiology and Pathophysiology, , ,"}]}},{"fullName":"Engel AK","lastName":"Engel","firstName":"Andreas","initials":"AK","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4899-8466"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurophysiology and Pathophysiology, , ,"}]}},{"fullName":"Nolte G","lastName":"Nolte","firstName":"Guido","initials":"G","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurophysiology and Pathophysiology, , ,"}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4899-8466"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics"]},"pubYear":"2025","abstractText":"Cross-bispectral measures provide a rich description of interactions in EEG signals, but their third-order tensor structure poses substantial challenges for interpretation and dimensionality reduction. We introduce a low-rank tensor decomposition framework specifically designed for cross-bispectral EEG data. The model expresses the bispectrum as a product of a single spatial mixing matrix and a compact source-interaction tensor, yielding a structured and interpretable representation of the data. Unlike classical tensor decompositions such as Tucker and its special case PARAFAC, where either the core tensor is unconstrained or restricted to rank-one terms, our formulation incorporates a source-space interpretation directly through the tensor  Q mnp , making the decomposition well suited for identifying dominant coupling components. After obtaining the low-rank representation, spatial demixing is performed using MOCA to derive clear and interpretable source maps. Through simulations, we show that the method consistently retrieves the dominant structure of the bispectrum across a wide range of conditions, including changes in SNR, dipole orientation, amplitude balance, and source complexity. Applied to resting-state EEG, the method produces anatomically plausible parietal generators associated with the strongest alpha-band bispectral interactions. Overall, the framework provides a principled and computationally efficient approach for reducing and interpreting cross-bispectral EEG data, offering source-level insights that are difficult to obtain using standard tensor factorization techniques.","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Preprint"]},"bookOrReportDetails":{"publisher":"bioRxiv","yearOfPublication":2025},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"European Research Council","grantId":"101097402","orderIn":0}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.64898/2025.12.21.695795"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/article/PPR/PPR1230389"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/api/fulltextRepo?pprId=PPR1230389&type=FILE&fileName=EMS214651-pdf.pdf&mimeType=application/pdf"}]},"commentCorrectionList":{"commentCorrection":[{"source":"MED","id":"41839270","reference":"Journal of neuroscience methods. 2026 Jul;431:110739","type":"Preprint of","note":"CrossRef Pre-print loader","orderIn":10001}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"N","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by-nc-nd","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"Y","nihAuthMan":"N","manuscriptId":"EMS214651","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCreation":"2026-05-19","firstPublicationDate":"2025-12-23","firstIndexDate":"2026-05-19","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-06-24","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}
